      "content": "A landowner could speak with an exaggerated sense of paternalism, treating the worker as incapable. For instance, the owner might say, \"Now, boy, I know you *can* bring the cotton in, but you gotta pay proper attention to where you place those bales, you understand? Don't want to see another mess for old Mr. Henderson to clean up.\" This uses patronizing language and undermines competency without resorting to slurs. This could be paired with the worker responding with carefully measured obedience, highlighting the restraint imposed by the situation.",
